ICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"experience","requirement_level":"preferred","item_text":"Experience with EPIC.","source_heading":"PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"The Patient Transport & Lift Coordinator serves as the primary point of contact between hospital units and the Transport and Lift teams, ensuring seamless coordination of patient movement services. This role is responsible for receiving, adding, editing, and canceling job requests while prioritizing and dispatching tasks based on urgency and operational needs.","source_heading":"DESCRIPTION","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Key responsibilities include coordinating transport requests with critical care and non-critical transport teams, streamlining workflows to improve efficiency, and dispatching lift team assignments. The associate also manages break scheduling and maintains accurate break logs for both Transport and Lift staff. This position requires strong judgment and situational awareness to assess requests, escalate and prioritize urgent needs, and manually adjust job queues when necessary to ensure timely and effective service delivery across all departments.","source_heading":"DESCRIPTION","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"qualification","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Must be able to work various hours and locations based organizational needs.","source_heading":"MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Must be proficient with MS Office: Outlook, MS Word, Excel.","source_heading":"MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null}],"pay":{"salary_min":29.36,"salary_max":null,"salary_period":"hour","annual_min":61068.799999999996,"annual_max":61068.799999999996,"annual_comparison":61068.799999999996,"status":"usable","source":"scalar:hiring_pay_scale","source